  "content_text": "\r\n        \r\n        Add License Plates During Cycle Count Checkbox\r\n        On the Work Special Handling Window (Cycle Count Tab)\r\n        \r\n        This setting (when enabled) allows you to identify a new license plate to the system  when performing a cycle count for a location. \r\n         \r\n        Important: If you want to confirm less license plates than the system thinks exist in the location, then this checkbox will expose the Done button on RF so that you are not forced to count all of the license plates in order to complete the cycle count work.\r\n         \r\n         \r\n         \r\n        Notes\r\n        \r\n        - This setting is only available when you are using a License Plate Selection Method of user initiated. \r\n         \r\n        - When the user attempts to add a new license plate, the system will reference the user's cycle count preferences:\r\n        \r\n            If the license plate falls within the user's positive tolerance, then the system will add to the location the new license plate/item quantity. \r\n             If the license plate falls above the user's positive tolerance, then the system will set the count of this location to pending review.\r\n        \r\n        - You can have the system set all counts that involve new license plates to a pending review status using the Set New License Plates To Pending Review Checkbox.\r\n         \r\n        - The system will ignore this setting if you have the ability to add items during a count. Since you are always allowed to add license plates when adding an item to a location's count, this setting is not recognized.\r\n         \r\n    ",
  "search_text": "\r\n        \r\n        \nAdd License Plates During Cycle Count Checkbox\n\r\n        \nOn the Work Special Handling Window (Cycle Count Tab)\r\n        \n\r\n        \nThis setting (when enabled) allows you to identify a new license plate to the system  when performing a cycle count for a location. \n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \nImportant: If you want to confirm less license plates than the system thinks exist in the location, then this checkbox will expose the Done button on RF so that you are not forced to count all of the license plates in order to complete the cycle count work.\n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \nNotes\r\n        \n\r\n        \n- This setting is only available when you are using a License Plate Selection Method of user initiated. \n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \n- When the user attempts to add a new license plate, the system will reference the user's cycle count preferences:\n\r\n        \n\r\n            \nIf the license plate falls within the user's positive tolerance, then the system will add to the location the new license plate/item quantity. \n\n\n\n\n\r\n            \n If the license plate falls above the user's positive tolerance, then the system will set the count of this location to pending review.\n\r\n        \n\r\n        \n- You can have the system set all counts that involve new license plates to a pending review status using the Set New License Plates To Pending Review Checkbox.\n\r\n        \n \n\r\n        \n- The system will ignore this setting if you have the ability to add items during a count. Since you are always allowed to add license plates when adding an item to a location's count, this setting is not recognized.\n\r\n        \n \n\r\n    ",
